WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.534
-Now, we all love our pets,

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:05.267
and every pet owner thinks
that their pet is the best.

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.000
Well, I wanted to see
if that was true,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.167
so it's time for "Why Is
Your Pet Better Than Me?"

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.267
Here we go.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.501
-♪ Why is your pet
better than me? ♪

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.133
♪ Better than me ♪

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:18.400
Alright, let's meet
our first pet.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.300
Welcome. What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.400
Oh, I see somebody.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.734
-I'm Jessica Hentoff.
I'm from St. Louis, Missouri.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.667
-Yeah, hello!

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.133
Oh, we love St. Louis.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:31.634
Jessica, thank you for joining.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.667
And who do you have
with you there? Wow.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.868
-This is Miss Maple.
-Oh, Miss Maple.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.567
It is a pleasure to meet you,
Maple.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:43.000
Can you tell me, Jessica,
why is your pet better than me?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
-Because Miss Maple
can pack her own suitcase.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.501
[ Audience "Ohs" ]

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:51.167
-That's true. I really can't
pack my own suitcase, but --

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.601
She can pack her own suitcase?

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.467
Can we see it?

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.200
-Of course you can.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.234
-Alright.

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.567
Wow.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.133
-Maple.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:06.300
-They just loosened the travel
restrictions, so this is --

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.601
-Are you ready?

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:09.467
-Yeah, sure.
Drum roll, maybe?

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.000
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.133
-Back up.
Back up.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.501
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:20.734
Oh, my God.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.467
What?!

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.033
That is unbelievable.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.968
Maple, great job!

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:27.934
Jessica, Maple, great job.

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:29.267
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:32.200
Maple, let us see your --
your cute little face.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.901
Oh, fantastic job.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.567
Jessica, thank you very much.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:36.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.300
Nailed it.
Nailed it right there.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.167
Let's meet our next pet.

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:43.334
Hello. What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:47.133
-Hello. I'm Lynne, and I'm
from Derbyshire in England.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.667
-Oh, my goodness.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.534
This is --

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:53.234
Now, Lynne, you have a lot --

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:54.968
Seems like you have
a lot of pets there.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:57.934
Who is the gang there?

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:00.734
-I've got 10 toy poodles
altogether.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.434
They're all family.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:05.601
Mojo, in fact,
here is a grandma.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:09.734
And then I've got aunties,
uncles, daughters,

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:10.901
all sorts here.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.100
This is Pixie.
-Hi, Pixie.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.400
Yeah, Pixie is like,
"I want to do a trick, too."

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.968
But which one tonight is gonna
show off their talent?

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:24.000
-It's our little Mojo here
that is our trick dog.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.834
-Oh, wow, alright.
So this is --

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.234
Mojo, this is your big,
shining moment.

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.300
Mojo all the way from England.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.133
Mojo, why are you
better than me?

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:33.334
What's your trick, pal?

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:37.067
-Well, Mojo can play the piano
and sing.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.334
-Yeah, you're right.
Yeah, I can't do that.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:42.667
But I try.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:45.467
But, alright, let's hear Mojo
and see what we have.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.367
Whenever you're ready, Lynne.
Thank you so much.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.200
-Okay.
Mojo, Mojo, Moj.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.934
Come play
Play, play.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.801
[ Piano playing ]
Come play.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.067
Play, play.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.133
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.467
That's it.
That's all you need.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.267
Mojo, great job.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.234
[ Piano playing ]

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:04.634
[ Dog barking ]

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.534
-Sing. Sing.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.567
-Oh, my God.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.534
Playing all the hits.

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:13.467
Mojo, thank you
for playing the hits.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:14.901
I know people don't want
to play the hits.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:16.300
Thank you very much.
I appreciate it.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.467
Lynne, Lynne,
that was fantastic.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:20.000
Thank you very, very much.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.968
Now it's time to meet
our last pet.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.067
Hello. What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.534
-Hi. I'm Kelly from
Orange County, California.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:30.267
-Hey, Kelly from Orange County.

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:31.901
Yeah, we love ya.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.901
Kelly, who do you have there
with you?

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:36.334
-I have my pigs,
Norman and PigPig.

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:39.334
-Oh, my gosh.
And PigPig is great.

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:41.968
Now, I love the name PigPig.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:46.968
Kelly, why is PigPig and Norman
better than me?

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:49.000
-Well, I believe that
they're better than you

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.367
they they can drink a beer,
non-alcoholic beer,

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.701
in 30 seconds faster than you.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.167
[ Audience "Ohs" ]

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:59.067
-I've never drank
a non-alcoholic beer.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:01.767
[ Rim shot ]
Thank you very much.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:05.434
No, the pig can chug
a non-alcoholic beer

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:07.367
in 30 seconds?

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:09.300
I'd love to see this.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.868
-They're better than a frat boy.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.467
-Can we get 30 seconds
on the clock?

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.901
Roots?

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.501
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:20.300
Drink, drink, drink,
drink, drink.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.234
Whenever you're ready.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:23.601
-Go for it.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:29.067
-Yeah, go for it, buddy.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.501
Yeah, they love it!

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:31.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:35.300
Yeah, the party animals.
Oh, my God.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.033
Oh, my God!

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.934
-And what's beer
without some beer nuts?

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:47.901
-They are -- They are literally
party animals.

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.234
I love it so much.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.534
A great job to all
of our talented pets.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:52.968
If you have a pet you think
is better than me,

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:54.167
I want to see it.

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.901
Go to tonightshow.com/
whyisyourpetbetterthanme.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:57.968
Submit a video of your pet.

